      "observed": "U1 is assigned footprint Package_SO:SO-8_5.3x6.2mm_P1.27mm, a wider 5.3 x 6.2 mm SO-8 package, while the MAX3485 library part itself is an 8-pin SOIC-8 and its own footprint filter only allows SOIC*3.9x4.9mm*P1.27mm* (or DIP).",
      "expected": "U1 should use a narrow SOIC-8 footprint matching the MAX3485 package, e.g. Package_SO:SOIC-8_3.9x4.9mm_P1.27mm.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U1\") (value \"MAX3485\") (footprint \"Package_SO:SO-8_5.3x6.2mm_P1.27mm\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libpart (lib \"Interface_UART\") (part \"MAX3485\") ... (fp \"SOIC*3.9x4.9mm*P1.27mm*\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The PCB pads will be too wide for the actual MAX3485 SOIC-8 leads, so U1 may not solder reliably or make contact; the serial-servo interface would not function.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design is largely consistent with the specification, but U1 uses a wide SO-8 footprint that does not match the MAX3485's narrow SOIC-8 package, so serial-mode assembly would likely fail."
}

